String Fingering
================

This is the revived build of the StringFingering application. It computes
possible fingerings for violin chords and passages and displays them in a
Swing desktop interface.

Building and running
--------------------

Requirements:

* GNU Make
* JDK 11 or newer
* abcMaine.jar (the legacy ABC notation and score-rendering library)

The build looks for the notation library at ~/abc/abcMaine.jar by default.
From this directory, compile and launch the application with:

    make run

If the library is elsewhere, supply its location explicitly:

    make run ABCMAINE_JAR=/path/to/abcMaine.jar

Build without launching with `make build`. Generated class files are placed
under build/classes and are not committed to Git.

Opening a score
---------------

Drag one `.abc` file from the file manager and drop it anywhere on the main
application window. The score is loaded and analyzed immediately. Files can
also be opened with File -> Analyze ABC file; both paths accept ABC notation
files only.

For a guide to every main control, see `docs/controls.md` or choose
Help -> Controls inside the application. Every active button and menu item also
has mouseover help.

Using the application
---------------------

This is a small tutorial on how to use the StringFingering application.

To open a score, use the File menu. If you want to use anchors, do not forget to put Anchors On.

To go through the Score, use the right and left arrows under the Score. To clean up boards, either double-click on one (which will remove all at its right) or
go to Boards -> Reset Score and Panels.

To use the numerous Panels to go through followed fingerings (a trail), either use the Extend button or right-click on the right arrow. This will let fingerings as they are,
and enable to move on. Note that extend will try to keep the current fingering so that it is coherent; if it cannot, it will go to a coherent trail, and notice you
of the change.

The deeper arrows are there to go to the Start or End of the Score.

Clcik Solve to Extend repeatedly as much as you can.

NOTE: For the arrows, one you click on an arrow, you can use the keyboard arrows to parse easily. Note that this uses focus; the keyboard arrows will work for
the last set of arrows used, be it in the Score or the Control Panel.
